-- Oil flowing into a cell that holds only water.  A column of 20 cells is
-- split into two blocks of ten, each its own equilibration region: the upper
-- block is equilibrated at 250 bar and the lower at 155 bar, each with a water
-- zone at its base.  Layer 11, the top of the lower block, has a vertical
-- permeability of 100 mD, so the blocks equalise through a tight layer.
--
-- Once the pressures have met, the water of the upper zone sinks through the
-- oil of the lower block while oil rises into the cells above, which until
-- then hold water alone.  Within three years the water joins the lower water
-- zone and leaves behind the saturation at which it stops moving.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
